 "cells": [
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-md-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "# Quick Reference\n\nCheat sheets for the toolchain, the Crush language and CASM. Every code block that\ncan run is run by the guide's checker against crush-ast `v0.3.9`. Details live in\nthe chapters linked from each heading.\n\n## Command line ([Getting Started](https://docs.crushlang.org/getting-started.html))\n\n| Command | Does |\n|---|---|\n| `crush run FILE [flags]` | run a `.crush`, `.casm` (text) or `.cvm1` file |\n| `crush build FILE.crush` | compile to `.cvm1` |\n| `crush-run run FILE [flags]` | same as `crush run`; all the capability flags live here |\n| `crush-run caps` | list the capabilities of your build |\n| `crushc FILE.crush -o OUT.cvm1` | compile; `--emit casm\\|ast\\|types` prints a layer; `-C` only checks |\n| `crush-compile FILE.casm -o OUT.cvm1 --cap NAME` | assemble CASM text |\n| `crush-repl` | interactive REPL |\n\nCapability flags (everything is **off** unless you pass it): `--stdlib` `--fs`\n`--fs-root DIR` `--env` `--time` `--net` `--process` `--crypto` `--db PATH`\n`--graphics` `--bus` `--task` `--akg` `--polyglot` `--cap NAME`. Quotas:\n`--max-steps` (default 1,000,000), `--max-stack` (4,096), `--max-output` (1 MiB),\n`--max-call-depth` (256).\n\n## Language ([Syntax](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/syntax.html))\n\n### Variables and functions\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let x = 42\nlet name: String = \"Alice\"\n\nfn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {\n    return a + b\n}\n\nfn greet(who) {\n    print(\"Hello, \" + who)\n}\n\ngreet(name)\nprint(add(x, 1))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "appendix/quick_reference.md:29",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "Hello, Alice\n43\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-md-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "- Semicolons are optional. Comments are `//` and `#`. Strings use double quotes only.\n- A function returns a value only with `return`; falling off the end yields `null`.\n- `print(x)` takes exactly one argument; `io.print(a, b, …)` takes any number.\n- No `let mut`, no `T?` types, no lambdas (CRUSH-75), no working `import` (CRUSH-110).\n\n### Control flow ([Control Flow](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/control_flow.html))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-2",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let n = 3\nif n > 5 {\n    print(\"big\")\n} else if n > 1 {\n    print(\"medium\")\n} else {\n    print(\"small\")\n}\n\nlet i = 0\nwhile i < 2 {\n    i = i + 1\n}\n\nfor k in 0..3 {\n    print(k)\n}\n\nfor item in [\"a\", \"b\"] {\n    print(item)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "appendix/quick_reference.md:58",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "medium\n0\n1\n2\na\nb\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-md-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "`0..3` excludes the end. `break` and `continue` work in `while` and `for`.\n\n### Operators ([Operators](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/operators.html))\n\n`+ - * / %` · `== != < > <= >=` · `&& || !` (short-circuit) · unary `-` · pipeline `|>`.\nThere is no `and`/`or`/`not`, `**`, `//`, `+=` or ternary.\n\n### Errors\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "appendix-quick-reference-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "try {\n    throw \"disk full\"\n} catch e {\n    print(\"caught: \" + e)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "appendix/quick_reference.md:101",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "caught: disk full\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
